  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 130 PM MST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nNorthwest flow moderates through the day Sunday, with more westerly flow\nin the forecast trough early next week, leading to warmer and drier \nconditions areawide. Latest longer range model and ensemble data supports\na split flow pattern developing early next week, with an eastern Pacific \nsystem within the southern stream expected to move onshore across the \nsouthern California Coast on Tuesday. Model solutions differ on where \nthis system moves from there, with the GFS remaining the furtherest\nsouth with the system as it moves across the southern Rockies, where\nas the Canadian and EC solutions have it further north, bringing the\npotential for a more significant winter weather system for south central \nand southeast Colorado in the later Wednesday and Thursday \ntimeframe. Time will tell, if we see the first snowfall across \nsoutheast Colorado later next week.",
